{
    "dialogues": [
        {
            "character": "",
            "dialogue": "In this world, there exists humans and the robots that serve them.",
            "textSpeed": 0.075
        },
        {
            "character": "",
            "dialogue": "With today's advanced technology, robots are able to attend to all the needs a human may have.",
            "textSpeed": 0.075
        },
        {
            "character": "",
            "dialogue": "Robots can be housemaids, firefighters, doctors... the possiblities are endless.",
            "textSpeed": 0.075
        },
        {
            "character": "",
            "dialogue": "However, all robots have Three Laws they must abide by.",
            "textSpeed": 0.075
        },
        {
            "character": "",
            "dialogue": "First, a robot shall never injure a human being or allow a human being to come to harm;",
            "textSpeed": 0.075
        },
        {
            "character": "",
            "dialogue": "Second, unless they conflict with the First Law, a robot must obey their human's orders;",
            "textSpeed": 0.075
        },
        {
            "character": "Virgo",
            "dialogue": "(Huh...?)",
            "textSpeed": 0.05
        },
        {
            "character": "",
            "dialogue": "And finally, so long as there is no conflict with the First or Second Law, a robot must protect its own existence.",
            "textSpeed": 0.075
        },

        {
            "character": "Virgo",
            "dialogue": "(The Three Laws? Of course, I know those. I'm a mechanic, after all. But... why...?)",
            "textSpeed": 0.05
        },
        {
            "character": "",
            "dialogue": "Error is not error.",
            "textSpeed": 0.075
        },
        {
            "character": "",
            "dialogue": "Error.",
            "textSpeed": 0.095
        },
        {
